# Whitelist approach: ignore EVERYTHING, then re-include only the source files we want tracked.
# This keeps PyCharm's .idea/, __pycache__/, the shared-package symlinks (HelpersPackage.py, Log.py,
# PDFHelpers.py, Locale.py, FanzineDateTime.py, FanzineIssueSpecPackage.py), the generated Reports/,
# the big fancyPagesDictByWikiname.json, and the mklinks*.bat files out of git automatically -- so
# PyCharm's Commit no longer offers them.
#
# To track a new file, add another "!name" line for it below.
*
!.gitignore
!ConInstanceInfo.py
!Conventions.py
!F3Page.py
!F3Reference.py
!FancyAnalyzer.py
!LocalePage.py
!ScanF3PagesForConInfo.py
